ls/7906","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7906","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7906.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7906.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-09T01:47:02Z"},"body":"Closes #5844.\n\nDecision record for the #5678 knowledge-layer attachments & media cluster, written after its hard dependency resolved: #6435 closed completed 2026-11-09 and its feature matrix landed on main via PR #7887.\n\n`doc/knowledge-layer-attachments-media-5844.md` records, with matrix evidence and rejected alternatives:\n\n- **File handling — ADOPT** attachments as first-class addressable resources (Joplin/Logseq shape); references not copies; size caps as sync/deployment policy, not model property.\n- **OCR/handwriting — ADAPT** mobile capture as attachment resources + local/on-user-infrastructure OCR derivative objects; server-side indexing by default rejected (an index is a read path under the #5678 order).\n- **PDF annotation — ADAPT** Logseq's attachment-native shape; annotations are separate objects, source PDF immutable.\n- **Export — REJECT** silent payload drops; exports state exclusions before running and carry a payload manifest.\n\nPreserves #5678's ruled read-authority resolution order (object → user default → server config → public) and records 7 implementation invariants for the #2048 object model. Design only; no code changes.\n\nTask 13062 · lane code-n\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796780726&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7906&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7906&signature=f9e8287c7fccf47df21d6a07b23e2e9abe5fe7f2117349fcc64fe09583406af3\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-c